{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact R16 head 6303c2abf50d5ee1a7d856ec1ca4fd813f208614 on builder/publication-paths-r16-20261109, tree 00310fb9, all 9 artifacts, for request b300dca1 under promise d107501f and review request 012818a6. Before the provider push, the destination host now refuses an application file publication that touches a reserved control path, on every existing pin. The recorded outcome keeps its existing shape.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- Placement. The check runs in `#write` only for a `file-publication` target, after the existing `allowed()` setup and before `provider.send`. A malformed base, tree or path returns null, so nothing is sent. After the two awaits, the policy read and the inspection, `allowed()` checks the exact source and the private credential again before the push.\n- Reserved paths. `PUBLICATION_RESERVED` is `.github`, `.github/**`, `CODEOWNERS`, `docs/CODEOWNERS` and `RULES_PATTERNS`, which covers every `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. `publicationRefusal` classifies the requested path together with every path in the inspected change set. It uses the existing `classify`, links and unreadable count. So an alias into a control path refuses, an unchanged requested control path refuses, and an unresolved alias refuses.\n- Current Rules extents. `publicationExtents` accepts only an answer for the exact recorded Rules scope (and incarnation when recorded) that names an extents digest. Exactly one retained value of a known extents domain must hash to that digest, and its bytes must be canonical and bounded. An extent named `rules` or of class `authority` is then reserved. A missing, mismatched or unreadable policy returns null, and the host sends nothing. The check fails closed.\n- Production wiring. `DeployedScope` passes `snapshotReaderOf(scopes)` to `outsideOf`, which gives the reader to both `gitHubOutside` and `artifactsOutside`. `snapshotReaderOf.rules` reads `observe({of, asked: \"rules\"})` from the Rules scope. The Native witness uses the same `snapshotReaderOf` through the test host.\n- Evidence shape. A refusal answers `refused` with `{send: \"not-sent\", seen: \u003cactual head\u003e}`, the existing outcome body. The diagnostic travels beside it as `DestinationAnswer.refusal` and never enters the recorded evidence. No Native rule, pin, outcome shape or setting changes.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main ce0290fb is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 9 paths that its 9 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 11 checked, 0 flagged.\n- The seals. I recomputed both outside the builder's worktree. destination-host.ts gives 421493f1… and publication-policy.ts gives e2594477…, each equal to its literal. No route check, authority check or check order moves.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at c96996de: \"exit 0\". All five stages passed. The classification reads Node 142, Counting 56, Plain 4,028 plus 1 skip, and Native 1,122 plus 2 skips, with no issues or report errors and the source unchanged. After the gate, only the note and the gate manifest change.\n- The tests. The pure owner covers reserved paths and aliases, ordinary paths that stay open (`docs/AGENTS.md.txt`, `other/CODEOWNERS`, `.github-other/x.yml`), and the bounded, exact Rules value. Three Native cases cover the raw historical, trusted-package historical and current device-package pins. Each refuses a workflow, the instructions, both CODEOWNERS paths and a custom Rules authority path. Each case checks the unchanged ref, the push count, `host-refused`, the two-key evidence body and the separate diagnostic. Ordinary files and an unchanged Lending shelf page still publish, and replay stays consistent.\n- The control. At 242fc152, replacing only the host-policy call with an allowed result makes all three Native cases publish `.github/workflows/x.yml` and fail the aborted-state assertion at line 159. Both pure cases pass. The original verifier exited 1 because Vitest abbreviated the JSON message. The reconciliation over the same run's stderr exits 0 and keeps the verifier's failure on record. Packages and scripts at the head equal 242fc152.\n- The evidence. The pre-gate and gate manifests hash to a23da309… and bde4cd79…, the values that the note cites. Their 75 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. The note keeps the failed compiler and the two failed fixture units as failures.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The policy is a pure host owner that reuses the existing Git inspection and extent classifier. The host consults it at the one point before the push. Kernel section 7: this is a filed R1–R16 security fix in host code, it adds no kernel item, and section 7.1's exception covers it.\n\nSecurity: no finding. An application can no longer write workflows, ownership files, agent instructions or the room's own Rules control paths, directly or through an alias. A room whose Rules policy cannot be read publishes nothing instead of publishing unchecked. One limit holds by design, and docs/application-views.md states it: until declared prefixes arrive, one application can still overwrite another's ordinary file.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThe planner deploys after landing. No setting changes. This approval authorizes no deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc103277ce0125aff0fdf37cbfa7c1adb2a05ea2","binding":"assigned","head":"6303c2abf50d5ee1a7d856ec1ca4fd813f208614","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:065d20adcb8e7b5b81a616dd785b6b0442d7751b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d107501f110b3999dded992f08676cf0722243b6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f250931fb7405d428f4f688a1006dd9885bed447","review_path"